          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            This chapter introduces a generalized kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            equipped with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            or, with an eye towards their generalization to
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+smooth+homotopy+types"} smooth homotopy types
            %em
              smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            or
            %em
              smooth
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+0-types"} 0-types
            = succeed "." do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          %p
            The definition (Def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSpace"}
            below) subsumes that of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fr%C3%A9chet+manifolds"} Fréchet manifolds
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            but is both simpler and more powerful: smooth sets are simply
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gros+site"} gros site
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+Spaces"} Cartesian Spaces
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartSpCategory"}
            below) and as such form a nice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            – a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            – and this contains as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategories"} full subcategories
            the more “tame” objects such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#InclusionOfSmoothManifoldsIntoSmoothSets"}
            below) and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            (Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets"}
            below).
          %p
            In fact smooth sets are an early stage in a long sequence of generalized smooth spaces appearing in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
