              of morphisms the ordinary composition of functions of underlying sets.
          #DiffeologicalSpacesAreTheConcreteSmoothSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_15 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
                are the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+object"} concret
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
              (Def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfSmoothSets"}
            %p
              Moreover, in terms of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+topos"} cohesive
              structure on the category of smooth sets from Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsFormACohesiveTopos"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#CohesiveModalities"}> this def.
              ) among the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpace
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi SmoothSet
                      %mi conc
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mphantom
                        %mi AAAA
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DiffeologicalSpace
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    SmoothSet_{conc}
                    \\overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    SmoothSet
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_10 Proof
            %p First observe that the assignment of sets of plots
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \mapsto \mathbf{X}(U)
            %p
              of a diffeological space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
              constitutes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#Sheaf"}> this Def.
              ) on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EuclOp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EuclOp
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subsets"} open subsets
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+spaces"} Euclidean spaces
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsAreSheavesOnCartSp"}
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the third clause in the list of properties in Def.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
                  says that the assignment of sets of plots is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              %li
                %p
                  the second clause in the list of properties says that this presheaf satisfies the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf condition
              %li
                %p while the first clause in the list of properties is an extra condition, singling out diffeological spaces among all sheaves.
            %p
              Under this identification, the definition of a smooth map of diffeological spaces in Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
              says that it is equivalently a morphism of presheaves of sets of plots between sheaves of sets of plots, and hence a morphism of sheaves. This establishe a
              = succeed "-inclusion" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpace
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi EuclOp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DiffeologicalSpace
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Sh(EuclOp)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But by Prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#EquivalentSitesForCartSp"}
              the restriction from the site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi EuclOp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} EuclOp
              of all open subsets of Euclidean spaces to that of just the site
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
              between the corresponding
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi DiffeologicalSpace
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi EuclOp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CartSp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi SmoothSet
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    DiffeologicalSpace
                    \\hookrightarrow
                    Sh(EuclOp)
                    \\simeq
                    Sh(CartSp)
                    \\simeq
                    SmoothSet
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the last equivalence is Prop.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsAreSheavesOnCartSp"}
            %p
              It remains to see that under this inclusion, the diffeological spaces are identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+objects"} concrete objects
              among the smooth set.
            %p
              By definition (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#CohesiveModalities"}> this Def.
              ), a smooth set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X} \in SmoothSet
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concrete+object"} concrete
              = succeed "-unit" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sharp+modality"} sharp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %msubsup
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                          %mo ♯
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mo ♯
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X}
                    \\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_X^\sharp \phantom{A}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    \\sharp \mathbf{X}
                    \\,,
            %p
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#AdjunctionUnitFromHomIsomorphism"}> this Def.
              ) of the
              = succeed "-adjunction" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi coDisc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma \dashv coDisc)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X}
                    \\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_X \phantom{A}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    coDisc \Gamma \mathbf{X}
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now a morphism of sheaves is a monomorphism, precisely if for each object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
              in the site, its component function
            #eq:DecohesAsGammacoDiscUnit.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (8)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %msubsup
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                          %mo ♯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi coDisc
                    %mi Γ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X}(U)
                    \\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_X^\sharp(U) \phantom{A}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    (coDisc \Gamma \mathbf{X})(U)
            %p
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective function
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#RecognitionOfEpimorphisms"}> this Prop.
              ). Unde the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            #eq:CodiscretePlotIdentidification.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi SmoothSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ♯
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi Hom
                                    %mi SmoothSet
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi y
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi U
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ,
                                  %msubsup
                                    %mi η
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ♯
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ↓
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ↘
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mover
                                  %mrow
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi η
                                      %mi X
                                      %mo ♯
                                    %mo ∘
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo ˜
                          %mtd
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi coDisc
                            %mi Γ
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi SmoothSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi coDisc
                            %mi Γ
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Γ
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo ˜
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathbf{X}(U) &amp;\simeq&amp; Hom_{SmoothSet}(y(U), \mathbf{X})
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{ \eta_X^\sharp(U) }}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    {}^{\mathllap{ Hom_{SmoothSet}(y(U), \eta_X^\sharp ) }}\big\downarrow
                    \&amp;\searrow^{\mathrlap{ \widetilde{\eta^\sharp_X \circ (-)} }}&amp;
                    \\\
                    (coDisc \Gamma \mathbf{X}(U))
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    Hom_{SmoothSet}( y(U), coDisc \Gamma \mathbf{X} )
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    Hom_{Set}( \Gamma y(U), \Gamma \mathbf{X} )
                    \&amp;\simeq&amp;
                    Hom_{Set}( U, X )
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \phi &amp;\mapsto&amp; \widetilde \phi
                    \\,,
                    }
            %p
              where we first used the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#YonedaLemma"}> this Prop.
              ), then the adjunction isomorphism (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#eq:HomIsomorphismForAdjointFunctors"}> here
              ) of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊣
                      %mi coDisc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Gamma \dashv coDisc)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SmoothSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSet
              comes from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
              being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+site"} cohesive site
              (Prop.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SmoothSetsFormACohesiveTopos"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
              is given by evaluation on the point (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#CohesiveGlobalSectionsGivenByPointEvaluation"}> here
              ), and we wrote
            #eq:UnderlyingSetOfDiffeologicalSpaceAsSmoothSet.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Γ
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \;\coloneqq\; \Gamma \mathbf{X} = \mathbf{X}(\ast)
            %p
              for the set of points in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              is indeed a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+space"} diffeological space
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
            %p
              This shows that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DecohesAsGammacoDiscUnit"} (8)
              being an injection means equivalently that we have an injection of the form
            #eq:RearrangedDecohesAsGammacoDiscUnit.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (11)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mrow
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                        %msubsup
                          %mi η
                          %mi X
                          %mo ♯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mphantom
                          %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X}(U)
                    \\overset{\phantom{A} \eta_X^\sharp(U) \phantom{A}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    Hom_{Set}(U, X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}(U)
              is always a subset of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              to the set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DiffeologicalSpace"}
            %p
              This shows that every concrete smooth set is a diffeological space. For the converse, it remains to check that if we start with a diffeological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{X}
              with prescribed inclusion function
            #eq:DiffeologicalInclusionFunction.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (12)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{X}(U) \hookrightarrow Hom_{Set}(U,X)
            %p
              then
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:RearrangedDecohesAsGammacoDiscUnit"} (11)
              indeed reproduces this inclusion.
            %p
              To see this, first notice that, by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+categories+and+toposes#YonedaLemma"}> this prop.
              ) and the definition of smooth maps between diffeological spaces, the inclusion function
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DiffeologicalInclusionFunction"} (12)
              equals the component function of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi SmoothSet
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \;\colon\; SmoothSet \to Set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi SmoothSet
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Hom
                              %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Γ
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Γ
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %mi Γ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{y(U),\mathbf{X}}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\array{
                    Hom_{SmoothSet}( y(U), \mathbf{X} )
                    \&amp;\hookrightarrow&amp;
                    Hom_{Set}( \Gamma y(U), \Gamma \mathbf{X} )
                    \\\
                    f &amp;\mapsto&amp; \Gamma(f)
                    }
            %p
              Hence, by
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DecohesAsGammacoDiscUnit"} (8)
            #eq:PostcompositionWithEtaAsGamma.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (13)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi X
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Gamma_{y(U), \mathbf{X}} \;=\;  \widetilde{\eta_{\mathbf{X}} \circ (-)}
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this holds as a general fact about
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunctions"} adjunctions
              (a special case of
              = succeed ")." do
